course: dictionary
lesson: 12037
title: Cinematic: like a film
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cinematic comes from cinema, the place where films are shown. It has two meanings. The first is to do with films and the cinema: «Our cinematic lesson looked at how cameras move.» The second is more common in everyday talk: it means something looks or feels like a film, exciting and grand.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The sunset over the mountains was so cinematic that everyone stopped to take a photo.» A sunset is not a film, but the huge, beautiful view feels like a scene from one. So cinematic means grand and dramatic, like a film.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The game had cinematic effects, with huge explosions and soaring music.» Could you say «film-like effects» instead? Yes, so cinematic means like a film.
fact: Cinema means a place where films are shown, and also the art of making films.
fact: «Cinematic» means to do with films and the cinema.
fact: «Cinematic» also means looking or feeling like a film: exciting and grand, with big scenes and music.
fact: A «cinematic view» is a stunning view that looks like a scene from a film.
fact: Useful phrases: «cinematic experience» and «cinematic effects».
exercise: «The game had cinematic effects, with huge explosions.» What does cinematic mean here? | Very quiet and small | Wet and grey | *Like a film, big and exciting | Made of wood
exercise: Ruby says the sunset was cinematic. What does she mean? | It was a cinema ticket | *It looked grand and beautiful, like a film scene | It was dull and grey | It was very cold
exercise: «The cinematic lesson showed how a camera zooms in on a face.» What is the lesson about? | Maths tables | Football scores | Cooking dinner | *Films and how they are made
test: «We sat in the dark for the cinematic experience, with a huge screen and loud music.» What does cinematic experience suggest? | *A grand, film-like experience | A quick trip to the shops | A boring day at home | A walk in the rain
test: Which phrase means a grand, film-like view? | A broken view | A grey view | A silent view | *A cinematic view
exam: Which sentence uses cinematic to mean to do with films? | *«Our cinematic club studies how movies are made.» | «The cinematic cat slept all day.» | «The cinematic rain fell on the bus.» | «I had cinematic toast for breakfast.»
